---
import Post from "../../../layouts/Post.astro";
import RunningRecordNav from "../../../components/RunningRecordNav.astro";
import results from "../../../data/running/race-results.json";
import bests from "../../../data/running/personal-bests.json";
const frontmatter = {
  title: "Personal bests and race history",
  description: "My best known running marks in one place, with paces, World Athletics points, dates and the race or training context behind them.",
  updated: "2026-10-10",
};
const groups = [
  { kind: "track", title: "Track races", intro: "The men's national championships in June and U20 championships in July were separate meets. Placings below are the official combined classifications, rather than places within a heat." },
  { kind: "park", title: "5kmrun and XL park races", intro: "Distances follow the organizer's edition-specific descriptions. They are race records, without an added claim of certified course length." },
  { kind: "kids", title: "Kids Run", intro: "The two organized 2 km races are separate from the remembered sixth-grade neighbourhood effort." },
  { kind: "sofia", title: "Sofia Marathon: short-distance events", intro: "Times below are chip times. The distance is the label in each edition's official results; the races are the short-distance event, rather than the full marathon." },
  { kind: "marathon", title: "Marathon", intro: "The official chip time is the result. Recorded GPS distance and device time stay with the activity account." },
];
const date = (value) => new Date(`${value}T12:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString("en-GB", { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric", timeZone: "UTC" });
const time = (seconds, decimals = 1) => {
  const factor = 10 ** decimals;
  const units = Math.round(seconds * factor);
  const whole = Math.floor(units / factor);
  const hours = Math.floor(whole / 3600);
  const minutes = Math.floor(whole % 3600 / 60);
  const remainder = String(whole % 60).padStart(2, "0");
  const fraction = decimals ? `.${String(units % factor).padStart(decimals, "0")}` : "";
  return `${hours ? `${hours}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, "0")}` : minutes}:${remainder}${fraction}`;
};
const pace = (best) => best.seconds.map((seconds) => time(seconds * 1000 / best.distanceMeters, 0)).join("–");
const points = (best) => best.score?.points.join("–") ?? "—";
---
<Post frontmatter={frontmatter}>
  <RunningRecordNav />
  <p>
    My best known marks are organized by discipline, from 300 m to the marathon.
    Races, time trials and training efforts keep their settings; same-pace
    comparisons carry an asterisk and show the original distance and time.
    The results come from different years. The notebook keeps the
    {" "}<a href="/running-notebook/#the-runner-i-am-trying-to-build">800+ point goal profile</a>{" "}
    I am working toward now.
  </p>
  <p>
    Points use the men's columns of the
    {" "}<a href={bests.source}>2025 revised World Athletics tables</a>, with the lower
    score between thresholds. A time links to its source; the date leads to the
    account or activity. Pace is rounded to the nearest second per kilometre;
    points use the original time or unrounded conversion.
    Dates marked UTC retain an unresolved local day from the export.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="#personal-bests">Personal bests</a>{" · "}
    <a href="#race-history">Race history</a>{" · "}
    <a href="#measurement-notes">Measurement notes</a>{" · "}
    <a href="#training-references">Training references</a>
  </p>
  <span id="race-bests"></span>
  <h2 id="personal-bests">Personal bests by discipline</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table class="bests" role="table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Discipline</th><th scope="col">Time<br /><span class="small">pace / km</span></th><th scope="col">Points</th><th scope="col">Date and setting</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody role="rowgroup">{bests.rows.map((best) => <tr id={best.id} role="row">
      <th scope="row" role="rowheader">{best.aliases?.map((id) => <span id={id}></span>)}{best.distance}</th>
      <td role="cell"><a class="mark" href={best.source}>{best.approximate && "~"}{best.time}</a>{best.score?.derived && <a href="#score-method" aria-label="Same-pace comparison">*</a>}<br /><span class="small">{pace(best)}</span></td>
      <td role="cell"><span class="mark">{points(best)}{best.shortTimingUnknown && <a href="#timing-method" aria-label="Training timing method unestablished">†</a>}</span></td>
      <td role="cell"><a href={best.note ?? best.source}>{date(best.date)}</a>{best.dateBasis === "utc" && <span class="small"> UTC</span>}<br />
        <span class="small">{best.kind} · {best.context}</span>
        {best.original && <><br /><span class="small">{best.score?.derived ? "Original" : "Whole run"}: {best.original.distance} in {best.original.time}</span></>}
      </td>
    </tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>
    * Same-pace comparisons retain the original distance and time; they do not
    establish another completed race or finish split. Sofia's short-course length
    remains unresolved. † Short training points are conditional on the unestablished
    timing method. The <a href="#measurement-notes">measurement notes</a> keep
    these limits and the scoring details together.
  </p>
  <h2 id="race-history">Race history</h2>
  <p>
    The full recovered race history follows. Original result times, course labels,
    placings and the dated accounts remain here, including earlier marks that were
    later improved. Chip times govern road results; gun times stay separately labelled.
  </p>
  {groups.map((group) => <section aria-labelledby={group.kind}>
    <h2 id={group.kind}>{group.title}</h2>
    <p>{group.intro}</p>
    <div class="tablewrap"><table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Date</th><th scope="col">Event</th><th scope="col">Time</th><th scope="col">Finish</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{results.filter((result) => result.kind === group.kind).sort((a,b) => a.date.localeCompare(b.date)).map((result) => <tr id={result.id}>
        <td><a href={result.note}>{date(result.date)}</a></td>
        <td>{result.event}<br />{result.distance.split(/([¹²])/).map((part) =>
          part === "¹" ? <a href="#park-distance-note" aria-label="Park-course distance note">¹</a> :
          part === "²" ? <a href="#sofia-distance-note" aria-label="Sofia course-distance note">²</a> : part
        )}</td>
        <td><a href={result.source}>{result.time}</a>{result.gunTime && <><br /><span class="dim">Gun {result.gunTime}</span></>}</td>
        <td>{result.place}</td>
      </tr>)}</tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>)}
  <h2 id="measurement-notes">Measurement and score notes</h2>
  <p id="score-method">
    * A comparison keeps the original effort's average pace over the named
    discipline. The mile scales the documented 1600 m in 5:08 to 1609.344 m;
    its comparison is 5:09.80, worth 388 points. The road comparisons scale
    longer source distances down, using full elapsed time for recordings.
    They do not establish an additional completed race or finish split.
    Displayed comparison times round up to the event table's precision.
    Sofia's course length remains unresolved: 291 points uses the official
    results' 10.5 km label; 42:04 over 10 km would give 205.
  </p>
  <p>
    The 15 km time sums the first fifteen 1 km watch laps. Its distance is
    recorded by the device. The 20 km comparison also uses a GPS distance,
    without a claim of a measured course. The half-marathon best is the
    reported 1:36:57 training split within the April 24.64 km outing,
    replacing the earlier whole-run pace comparison;
    the separate{" "}<a href="/running/record/2023-2025/#autumn-2024-more-long-running">October 21.10 km in 1:38:14</a>{" "}
    remains in the dated account. The 2000 m and 3000 m training paces both
    round to 3:26/km; their unrounded difference is 0.3 seconds/km.
  </p>
  <p id="timing-method">
    † Short training points compare the written mark. The short efforts' timing method,
    start and wind have not been established. Official comparison of hand-timed
    sprints at 300–400 m requires adding 0.14 seconds;
    for example, a hand-timed 56.05 would be scored as 56.19, giving 531 rather
    than the literal mark's 537.
  </p>
  <h3 id="park-distance-note">Park-course labels</h3>
  <p>
      ¹ North Park's current result page says 6.0 km. The organizer's
      <a href="https://info.5kmrun.bg/4096-2/">report published on 7 December 2015</a>
      describes the same short event as 5 km. I retain that contemporary label;
      no exact historical course measurement has been recovered.
    </p>
  <h3 id="sofia-distance-note">The Sofia short-course label</h3>
  <p>
        ² The 2020 results say 10 km; the 2021 results say 10.5 km, while that
        edition's map advertises 10 km. I remember the same route in those two
        years. The exact measured length of the separate short course remains
        unresolved, so the 42:04 is not listed as a certified 10,000 m best.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="https://sofia2018.bg/2017/10/10/%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%82-%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BA%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B4%D0%B8-%D0%BD%D0%B0-wizz-air-%D1%81%D0%BE%D1%84%D0%B8%D1%8F-%D0%BC/">2017 instructions</a>
        describe one short lap of the older four-lap marathon route, starting
        outside Vasil Levski National Stadium. The later start was
        <a href="https://www.sofia.bg/en/w/izvestni-atleti-pristigat-za-wizz-air-sofia-maraton-sledvasata-nedela">Battenberg Square</a>;
        the <a href="https://www.sofia.bg/bg/web/guest/w/sofijskiat-maraton-startira-v-nedela-10-oktomvri">2021 maps</a>
        show a two-lap marathon and a separate shorter loop. Dividing the
        marathon distance by four would not recover the later short-course length.
      </p>
  {bests.retiredAnchors.map((id) => <span id={id}></span>)}
  <h2 id="training-references">Training references</h2>
  <p>
    Other sprint distances and interval lengths stay with the dated training
    record. The discipline table above keeps the selected best marks. Other dated
    references stay with their accounts: the
    <a href="/running/record/early/">childhood neighbourhood effort</a>, the
    <a href="/running/record/2020/#30-december--a-reported-2-km-in-715">reported 2 km in 2020</a>
    and the
    <a href="/running/record/2026/#27-september--2000-m-time-trial">current 2000 m trial</a>.
    Their dates, measurement limits and roles in the story remain visible there.
  </p>
  <p>
    Repeated workouts have a different comparison: times, count and recovery
    together. See the <a href="/running/record/2021/#the-repeated-900s">2021 900 m series</a>,
    <a href="/running/record/2022/#19-january--the-mixed-rest-fast-template">mixed-rest fast work in 2022</a>
    and <a href="/running/record/2026/#repeating-a-protocol">current protocol comparisons</a>.
  </p>
</Post>
<style>
  .bests th[scope="row"] { font-weight: 400; }
  .small { font-size: 11.5px; }
  .mark { white-space: nowrap; }
  .bests td:last-child { min-width: 115px; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .bests, .bests thead, .bests tbody { display: block; }
    .bests tr { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 0 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 12px 0; }
    .bests th, .bests td { border: 0; padding: 0; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .bests thead th:last-child { display: none; }
    .bests tbody td:last-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; padding-top: 8px; min-width: 0; }
  }
</style>
